From fcd3787076ea28e96a31e85cee51e41c9f4fe6ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caokyhieu <caokyhieu253@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:48:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(index): tree/PiPNN centroid assignment and
 IVF_PIPNN_FLAT sub-index

Work in progress for the Lance index-build optimization plan.

- Carry the existing IVF_RQ build optimizations (blocked float32 L2
  assignment, GIST benchmark) as the baseline.
- Retain the hierarchical k-means routing tree (AssignmentTree) with
  greedy/beam assignment; retention leaves trained centroids unchanged.
- Add CentroidAssignment {Auto, Exact, Hnsw, Pipnn, Tree} plus seed,
  hierarchical_k and refine_iters to IvfBuildParams; explicit backends
  never fall back silently. Add PreparedAssignment for measurement.
- Add the optional `pipnn` feature: lance-pipnn C++ bridge over the fast
  PiPNN builder (exception-safe, NEON paths, portable flags by default,
  LANCE_PIPNN_NATIVE=1 opt-in) and a Rust PiPNN graph with beam search.
- PiPNN centroid assignment runs in parallel and rejects graphs that do
  not reach every centroid from the entry point.
- Register IVF_PIPNN_FLAT (float32 L2): build, persist, reopen, search.
  Remap, incremental and fresh-segment builds return NotSupported.
- Port SVE/SVE2 pairwise kernels with runtime dispatch on AArch64.
- Add lance-index-bench, a standalone benchmark runner (GIST/BIGANN,
  fixed-model and complete-build modes, per-query timing, assignment
  quality, raw JSONL/CSV outputs).
- Fix derive_ivf_params for the new IvfBuildParams fields.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
